        {
            "_id": "p52lQS3VKK447diy",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/TwoActions.webp",
            "name": "Aeon Star's Curse",
            "sort": 700000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 2
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>Deravon's ghost has four tiny motes of darkness that constantly orbit the glowing helm atop his head. When he activates the Aeon Star's Curse, one of these motes of darkness fires from its orbit to strike a living creature within 120 feet. That creature takes @Damage[5d6[spirit]] damage and must attempt a @Check[will|dc:28] save. An expended Aeon Star returns to its orbit around Deravon's head automatically after 1 hour has passed, but if no Aeon Stars orbit his head, Deravon's ghost can't activate Aeon Star's Curse, and the Athletics check to [[/act disarm]] his helm drops to DC 23.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes @Damage[2d6[spirit]] damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes @Damage[4d6[spirit]] damage and becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Stupefied]{Stupefied 1} with an unlimited duration.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes @Damage[8d6[spirit]] damage and becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Stupefied]{Stupefied 2} with an unlimited duration. In addition, they suffer from an overwhelming conviction that, at any moment, the Aeon Star might appear in the sky above, portending the end of all things. As long as they remain outdoors during the day or indoors or underground at any time of day, the cursed character is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Off-Guard] from this constant distraction. While outdoors at night, the cursed character is also @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Slowed]{Slowed 1} from this spiritual conviction.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [],
                "slug": "aeon-stars-curse",
                "traits": {
                    "value": [
                        "curse",
                        "divine",
                        "emotion",
                        "mental"
                    ]
                }
            },
            "type": "action"
        },
        {
