        {
            "_id": "OCpQqaQnTir9ueI4",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/TwoActions.webp",
            "name": "Slice of Death",
            "sort": 900000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 2
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>Deravon's ghost swings his ghostly longsword in an arc before him, unleashing a @Template[type:cone|distance:30] of void energy. Creatures in the area take @Damage[8d6[void]|options:area-damage] damage and must make a @Check[fortitude|dc:28] save against the following additional effects. Deravon's ghost can't use Slice Of Death for [[/gmr 1d4 #rounds]]{1d4 rounds}.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature takes no damage and is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and an additional @Damage[2d6[persistent,void]|options:area-damage] damage as their flesh begins to rot away.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage, @Damage[2d6[persistent,void]|options:area-damage] damage, and becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Slowed]{Slowed 1} as long as they continue taking the persistent void damage as their body begins to stiffen up as if from rigor mortis.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
